    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">Set in seventeenth-century Holland, this historical novel imagines the complex story behind one of Rembrandt&apos;s most famous paintings. Commissioned by a prominent Amsterdam medical guild, The Anatomical Lesson of Dr. Nicolaes Tulp was one of Rembrandt&apos;s first paintings to gain public notice; the novel opens on the morning of the medical dissection, and, as they prepare for that evening&apos;s big event, follows several characters, including Rembrandt himself.</marc:subfield>
